# v307a — CEREMONY WIRING
#
# An integration/equivalence release: the seven ceremonies are CREATE OR REPLACE'd
# to consume the frozen v306 admissibility authority instead of their own inline
# conditions. Externally observable behavior is preserved (equivalence slice); no
# Class-U closure (that is v307b), no occurrence-resolution pulled backward.
#
# The seven ceremonies keep their identity signatures (CREATE OR REPLACE), so no
# composed version guard changes. The only new object is the deployed marker; the
# wiring itself is proven by the permanent proof and the v306 differential
# regression run against the migrated ceremonies.
release          v307a
migration        supabase/v307a_wiring.sql
migration_source repository
min_release      v306

superseded       start_service (rewired to consume admissibility_evaluate)
superseded       close_event (rewired)
superseded       release_event (rewired)
superseded       release_occurrence (rewired)
superseded       assign_staff (rewired; Class-U kept inline)
superseded       correct_staffing_assignment (rewired; Class-U kept inline)
superseded       release_staffing_assignment (rewired; Class-U kept inline)

function         v307a_wiring()
